{t:"G",title:"Can / can't",intro:"<b>can</b> exprime la capacité, la possibilité et sert aussi à demander ou proposer poliment.",formsTitle:"Formes de can",forms:[["affirmatif","I can swim"],["négatif","I can't (cannot) swim"],["question","Can you swim?"],["après can","verbe SANS to"],["toutes personnes","he can, we can (invariable)"]],sections:[{h:"Toujours + verbe à la base",body:"Après can, jamais de « to » : <b>I can swim</b> (pas « I can to swim »). can ne change pas : he can, she can, we can."},{h:"Demander & proposer",body:"<b>Can you help me?</b> (peux-tu…?), <b>Can I open the window?</b> (puis-je…?). C'est plus direct que « could » (plus poli)."}],examples:[["I can speak English.","Je sais parler anglais."],["She can't come tonight.","Elle ne peut pas venir ce soir."],["Can you help me?","Peux-tu m'aider ?"],["He can drive a car.","Il sait conduire une voiture."],["We can meet tomorrow.","On peut se voir demain."],["Can I ask a question?","Puis-je poser une question ?"]],pitfalls:["« I can to swim » est faux → I can swim.","can ne prend jamais de -s : « he cans » est faux."],keypoints:["can = pouvoir / savoir faire.","Négatif : can't.","can + verbe sans to, invariable."],drills:[{q:"I ___ swim very well.",options:["can","can to","cans"],answer:"can",exp:""},{q:"She ___ come today.",options:["can't","doesn't can","not can"],answer:"can't",exp:""},{q:"___ you help me?",options:["Can","Do can","Are can"],answer:"Can",exp:""},{q:"He can ___ a car.",options:["drive","drives","to drive"],answer:"drive",exp:"Après can : base sans to."}],practice:[{en:"I can swim very well.",fr:"Je sais très bien nager.",hint:"swim"},{en:"She can speak three languages.",fr:"Elle parle trois langues.",hint:"speak"},{en:"Can you open the window?",fr:"Peux-tu ouvrir la fenêtre ?",hint:"window"},{en:"He can't drive yet.",fr:"Il ne sait pas encore conduire.",hint:"drive"},{en:"We can meet tomorrow.",fr:"Nous pouvons nous voir demain.",hint:"meet"},{en:"Can I ask a question?",fr:"Puis-je poser une question ?",hint:"question"},{en:"They can't come today.",fr:"Ils ne peuvent pas venir aujourd'hui.",hint:"today"},{en:"My dog can jump high.",fr:"Mon chien saute haut.",hint:"jump"},{en:"Can you hear me?",fr:"Tu m'entends ?",hint:"hear"},{en:"I can cook pasta.",fr:"Je sais cuisiner des pâtes.",hint:"cook"}]},
{"t":"V","title":"Les nombres et l’heure","intro":"Compter et dire l’heure sont indispensables pour donner un prix, un âge, un horaire ou un numéro.","formsTitle":"Nombres utiles","forms":[["one, two, three","un, deux, trois"],["ten / twenty","dix / vingt"],["a hundred","cent"],["first / second","premier / deuxième"],["What time is it?","Quelle heure est-il ?"],["It’s half past six","Il est six heures et demie"]],"sections":[{"h":"Dire l’heure","body":"On dit l’heure avec <b>it’s</b> : <b>it’s seven o’clock</b> (7h), <b>it’s a quarter past nine</b> (9h15), <b>it’s half past two</b> (2h30)."},{"h":"Demander","body":"<b>What time is it?</b> ou <b>Do you have the time?</b>. Pour un prix : <b>How much is it?</b>"}],"examples":[["I have two brothers.","J’ai deux frères."],["It’s ten o’clock.","Il est dix heures."],["The bus leaves at eight.","Le bus part à huit heures."],["She is twenty years old.","Elle a vingt ans."],["It costs five euros.","Ça coûte cinq euros."],["My room is number three.","Ma chambre est la numéro trois."]],"pitfalls":["Pour l’âge on utilise be : <b>I am 20</b>, pas « I have 20 ».","« o’clock » ne s’emploie qu’aux heures pile : seven o’clock, jamais « seven fifteen o’clock »."],"keypoints":["Nombres cardinaux pour compter, ordinaux pour classer.","It’s + heure.","How much pour un prix."],"drills":[{"q":"It’s ___ past six (6h30).","options":["half","quarter","o’clock"],"answer":"half","exp":"6h30 = half past six."},{"q":"She is 20 years ___.","options":["old","age","have"],"answer":"old","exp":"be + number + years old."},{"q":"___ time is it?","options":["What","How","When"],"answer":"What","exp":"What time is it?"},{"q":"It ___ five euros.","options":["costs","cost","is cost"],"answer":"costs","exp":"Présent simple : it costs."}],"practice":[{"en":"It’s nine o’clock.","fr":"Il est neuf heures.","hint":"clock"},{"en":"I have three cats.","fr":"J’ai trois chats.","hint":"three"},{"en":"The film starts at eight.","fr":"Le film commence à huit heures.","hint":"starts"},{"en":"How much is this?","fr":"Combien coûte ceci ?","hint":"much"},{"en":"She is thirty years old.","fr":"Elle a trente ans.","hint":"years"},{"en":"It’s half past ten.","fr":"Il est dix heures et demie.","hint":"half"},{"en":"We have two tickets.","fr":"Nous avons deux billets.","hint":"tickets"},{"en":"My number is seven.","fr":"Mon numéro est le sept.","hint":"number"},{"en":"The shop opens at nine.","fr":"Le magasin ouvre à neuf heures.","hint":"opens"},{"en":"It’s a quarter past five.","fr":"Il est cinq heures et quart.","hint":"quarter"}]},
{"t":"G","title":"Les articles : a, an, the","intro":"Les articles précèdent les noms. <b>a/an</b> = un/une (indéfini), <b>the</b> = le/la/les (défini).","formsTitle":"Quel article ?","forms":[["a book","un livre (consonne)"],["an apple","une pomme (voyelle)"],["an hour","une heure (h muet)"],["the sun","le soleil (unique)"],["the books","les livres"],["(rien)","noms pluriels généraux"]],"sections":[{"h":"a ou an ?","body":"On met <b>an</b> devant un <b>son</b> de voyelle : an apple, an egg, an hour (h muet). Sinon <b>a</b> : a car, a university (son « you »)."},{"h":"Quand utiliser the","body":"On utilise <b>the</b> pour une chose précise ou unique : <b>the</b> moon, <b>the</b> car I bought. Pas d’article pour les généralités : <b>I like music</b>."}],"examples":[["I have a dog.","J’ai un chien."],["She eats an orange.","Elle mange une orange."],["The sky is blue.","Le ciel est bleu."],["I need an umbrella.","J’ai besoin d’un parapluie."],["He plays the guitar.","Il joue de la guitare."],["Cats are cute.","Les chats sont mignons."]],"pitfalls":["On dit <b>an</b> hour (h muet) mais <b>a</b> university (son « you ») — c’est le son qui compte, pas la lettre.","Pas d’article pour parler en général : « I love the coffee » → « I love coffee »."],"keypoints":["a/an = indéfini singulier.","an devant un son de voyelle.","the = défini, chose précise ou unique."],"drills":[{"q":"I ate ___ apple.","options":["a","an","the"],"answer":"an","exp":"Son de voyelle → an."},{"q":"She has ___ car.","options":["a","an","the"],"answer":"a","exp":"Consonne → a."},{"q":"Look at ___ moon!","options":["a","an","the"],"answer":"the","exp":"Chose unique → the."},{"q":"Wait ___ hour, please.","options":["a","an","the"],"answer":"an","exp":"h muet → an."}],"practice":[{"en":"I have a question.","fr":"J’ai une question.","hint":"question"},{"en":"She is an artist.","fr":"Elle est artiste.","hint":"artist"},{"en":"Open the window, please.","fr":"Ouvre la fenêtre, s’il te plaît.","hint":"window"},{"en":"He wants an ice cream.","fr":"Il veut une glace.","hint":"cream"},{"en":"The dog is very big.","fr":"Le chien est très grand.","hint":"dog"},{"en":"I need a pen.","fr":"J’ai besoin d’un stylo.","hint":"pen"},{"en":"We watched the game.","fr":"Nous avons regardé le match.","hint":"game"},{"en":"She bought an egg.","fr":"Elle a acheté un œuf.","hint":"egg"},{"en":"The teacher is kind.","fr":"Le professeur est gentil.","hint":"teacher"},{"en":"I read a book every week.","fr":"Je lis un livre chaque semaine.","hint":"book"}]},
{"t":"V","title":"La famille","intro":"Le vocabulaire de la famille pour parler de tes proches et poser des questions simples.","formsTitle":"Les membres de la famille","forms":[["mother / father","mère / père"],["brother / sister","frère / sœur"],["son / daughter","fils / fille"],["parents","les parents"],["grandmother","grand-mère"],["husband / wife","mari / femme"]],"sections":[{"h":"La possession","body":"On ajoute <b>’s</b> pour dire à qui : <b>my brother’s car</b> (la voiture de mon frère), <b>Tom’s sister</b> (la sœur de Tom)."},{"h":"Poser des questions","body":"<b>Do you have</b> any brothers or sisters? — Yes, I have one sister."}],"examples":[["This is my mother.","Voici ma mère."],["I have two sisters.","J’ai deux sœurs."],["His father is a doctor.","Son père est médecin."],["Her brother is tall.","Son frère est grand."],["My parents live in Paris.","Mes parents vivent à Paris."],["Tom’s wife is French.","La femme de Tom est française."]],"pitfalls":["« brother » et « sister » ne changent pas au pluriel autrement qu’avec -s : brothers, sisters.","On dit « my parents », pas « my parent’s », pour parler des deux."],"keypoints":["Vocabulaire de base de la famille.","’s pour la possession.","Do you have…? pour demander."],"drills":[{"q":"My mother’s ___ is my father.","options":["husband","son","brother"],"answer":"husband","exp":"Le mari de ma mère = mon père."},{"q":"I have one ___ and two sisters.","options":["brother","brothers","brother’s"],"answer":"brother","exp":"one + singulier."},{"q":"This is ___ car (à Tom).","options":["Tom’s","Toms","Tom"],"answer":"Tom’s","exp":"Possession ’s."},{"q":"___ you have any sisters?","options":["Do","Are","Is"],"answer":"Do","exp":"Question au présent simple."}],"practice":[{"en":"This is my father.","fr":"Voici mon père.","hint":"father"},{"en":"I love my family.","fr":"J’aime ma famille.","hint":"family"},{"en":"Her sister is a nurse.","fr":"Sa sœur est infirmière.","hint":"sister"},{"en":"My grandmother is very kind.","fr":"Ma grand-mère est très gentille.","hint":"grandmother"},{"en":"Do you have any brothers?","fr":"As-tu des frères ?","hint":"brothers"},{"en":"His son is five years old.","fr":"Son fils a cinq ans.","hint":"son"},{"en":"My parents are teachers.","fr":"Mes parents sont professeurs.","hint":"parents"},{"en":"Tom’s daughter is here.","fr":"La fille de Tom est ici.","hint":"daughter"},{"en":"She is my wife.","fr":"C’est ma femme.","hint":"wife"},{"en":"We visit our grandparents.","fr":"Nous rendons visite à nos grands-parents.","hint":"grandparents"}]},
{"t":"G","title":"This, that, these, those","intro":"Les démonstratifs servent à montrer des choses selon leur distance et leur nombre.","formsTitle":"Proche ou loin, singulier ou pluriel","forms":[["this","ceci (proche, singulier)"],["that","cela (loin, singulier)"],["these","ceux-ci (proche, pluriel)"],["those","ceux-là (loin, pluriel)"]],"sections":[{"h":"La distance","body":"<b>this/these</b> = près de moi ; <b>that/those</b> = plus loin. <b>This</b> book (dans ma main) vs <b>that</b> book (là-bas)."},{"h":"Le nombre","body":"Singulier : <b>this/that</b>. Pluriel : <b>these/those</b>. This car / these cars."}],"examples":[["This is my phone.","Ceci est mon téléphone."],["That is your house.","C’est ta maison (là-bas)."],["These shoes are new.","Ces chaussures sont neuves."],["Those birds are singing.","Ces oiseaux (là-bas) chantent."],["I like this song.","J’aime cette chanson."],["Who are those people?","Qui sont ces gens là-bas ?"]],"pitfalls":["« these » et « those » sont pluriels : « these car » est faux → « these cars ».","La prononciation this /ɪ/ vs these /iː/ change le sens (singulier/pluriel)."],"keypoints":["this/that = singulier ; these/those = pluriel.","this/these = proche ; that/those = loin."],"drills":[{"q":"___ shoes are dirty (proche, pluriel).","options":["These","This","That"],"answer":"These","exp":"Proche + pluriel = these."},{"q":"Look at ___ mountain over there.","options":["that","this","these"],"answer":"that","exp":"Loin + singulier = that."},{"q":"I want ___ apple in my hand.","options":["this","these","those"],"answer":"this","exp":"Proche + singulier = this."},{"q":"Who are ___ people over there?","options":["those","these","that"],"answer":"those","exp":"Loin + pluriel = those."}],"practice":[{"en":"This is my seat.","fr":"C’est ma place.","hint":"seat"},{"en":"That car is expensive.","fr":"Cette voiture (là-bas) est chère.","hint":"car"},{"en":"These flowers smell nice.","fr":"Ces fleurs sentent bon.","hint":"flowers"},{"en":"Those clouds are dark.","fr":"Ces nuages (là-bas) sont sombres.","hint":"clouds"},{"en":"I like this colour.","fr":"J’aime cette couleur.","hint":"colour"},{"en":"That was a great day.","fr":"C’était une super journée.","hint":"great"},{"en":"These books are mine.","fr":"Ces livres sont à moi.","hint":"books"},{"en":"Give me that spoon.","fr":"Donne-moi cette cuillère.","hint":"spoon"},{"en":"This coffee is hot.","fr":"Ce café est chaud.","hint":"coffee"},{"en":"Those were the best years.","fr":"C’étaient les meilleures années.","hint":"years"}]},
{"t":"V","title":"Les couleurs et les objets du quotidien","intro":"Nommer les couleurs et les objets courants pour décrire ce qui t’entoure.","formsTitle":"Couleurs et objets","forms":[["red / blue / green","rouge / bleu / vert"],["black / white","noir / blanc"],["a table / a chair","une table / une chaise"],["a phone / a key","un téléphone / une clé"],["a bag / a bottle","un sac / une bouteille"],["a door / a window","une porte / une fenêtre"]],"sections":[{"h":"L’ordre des mots","body":"En anglais l’adjectif de couleur vient <b>avant</b> le nom : a <b>red</b> car (une voiture rouge), pas « a car red »."},{"h":"Décrire","body":"On utilise be : <b>The bag is blue.</b> — pour poser la question : <b>What colour is it?</b>"}],"examples":[["The car is red.","La voiture est rouge."],["I have a black bag.","J’ai un sac noir."],["Where is my phone?","Où est mon téléphone ?"],["The door is white.","La porte est blanche."],["She has green eyes.","Elle a les yeux verts."],["This is a blue bottle.","C’est une bouteille bleue."]],"pitfalls":["L’adjectif se place avant le nom : « a car red » est faux → « a red car ».","Les adjectifs ne prennent jamais de -s : « reds cars » → « red cars »."],"keypoints":["Couleur + nom (dans cet ordre).","be pour décrire une couleur.","What colour is it? pour demander."],"drills":[{"q":"I want a ___ car.","options":["red","car red","reds"],"answer":"red","exp":"Adjectif avant le nom."},{"q":"The keys ___ on the table.","options":["are","is","be"],"answer":"are","exp":"keys = pluriel → are."},{"q":"What ___ is your bag?","options":["colour","color is","coloured"],"answer":"colour","exp":"What colour is…?"},{"q":"She has ___ eyes.","options":["green","greens","green’s"],"answer":"green","exp":"Pas de -s aux adjectifs."}],"practice":[{"en":"My bag is black.","fr":"Mon sac est noir.","hint":"bag"},{"en":"I have a blue phone.","fr":"J’ai un téléphone bleu.","hint":"phone"},{"en":"The chair is white.","fr":"La chaise est blanche.","hint":"chair"},{"en":"Where are my keys?","fr":"Où sont mes clés ?","hint":"keys"},{"en":"She wears a green dress.","fr":"Elle porte une robe verte.","hint":"dress"},{"en":"The bottle is empty.","fr":"La bouteille est vide.","hint":"bottle"},{"en":"Close the window, please.","fr":"Ferme la fenêtre, s’il te plaît.","hint":"window"},{"en":"I like the red one.","fr":"J’aime le rouge.","hint":"red"},{"en":"The table is very old.","fr":"La table est très vieille.","hint":"table"},{"en":"His car is yellow.","fr":"Sa voiture est jaune.","hint":"yellow"}]},
{"t":"G","title":"Le pluriel des noms","intro":"La plupart des noms prennent -s au pluriel, mais certains suivent des règles particulières.","formsTitle":"Formes du pluriel","forms":[["cat → cats","règle générale : + s"],["bus → buses","-s/-ch/-sh/-x : + es"],["baby → babies","consonne + y : y → ies"],["knife → knives","-f/-fe : → ves"],["child → children","irrégulier"],["man → men","irrégulier"]],"sections":[{"h":"La règle du -es","body":"Après <b>s, ss, ch, sh, x</b> on ajoute <b>-es</b> : box → box<b>es</b>, watch → watch<b>es</b>."},{"h":"Les irréguliers","body":"À connaître par cœur : man/men, woman/women, child/children, foot/feet, tooth/teeth, person/people."}],"examples":[["I have three cats.","J’ai trois chats."],["There are two buses.","Il y a deux bus."],["The babies are sleeping.","Les bébés dorment."],["We need two knives.","Il nous faut deux couteaux."],["The children play outside.","Les enfants jouent dehors."],["Many people came.","Beaucoup de gens sont venus."]],"pitfalls":["« childs » et « mans » n’existent pas : children, men.","« people » est déjà pluriel : on dit « people are », jamais « peoples is »."],"keypoints":["Règle générale : + s.","+ es après s/ss/ch/sh/x.","Irréguliers à mémoriser."],"drills":[{"q":"One box, two ___.","options":["boxes","boxs","box"],"answer":"boxes","exp":"-x → + es."},{"q":"One child, two ___.","options":["children","childs","childrens"],"answer":"children","exp":"Irrégulier."},{"q":"One baby, three ___.","options":["babies","babys","babes"],"answer":"babies","exp":"consonne + y → ies."},{"q":"Many ___ were at the party.","options":["people","peoples","persons"],"answer":"people","exp":"people = pluriel de person."}],"practice":[{"en":"I have two dogs.","fr":"J’ai deux chiens.","hint":"dogs"},{"en":"There are five boxes.","fr":"Il y a cinq boîtes.","hint":"boxes"},{"en":"The men are working.","fr":"Les hommes travaillent.","hint":"men"},{"en":"My feet are cold.","fr":"J’ai froid aux pieds.","hint":"feet"},{"en":"The children are happy.","fr":"Les enfants sont heureux.","hint":"children"},{"en":"She has three watches.","fr":"Elle a trois montres.","hint":"watches"},{"en":"We saw many people.","fr":"Nous avons vu beaucoup de gens.","hint":"people"},{"en":"Brush your teeth.","fr":"Brosse-toi les dents.","hint":"teeth"},{"en":"The cities are big.","fr":"Les villes sont grandes.","hint":"cities"},{"en":"Two women arrived.","fr":"Deux femmes sont arrivées.","hint":"women"}]}
